    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system that maps to a level, and exposed both fields on the owner response.\n\n**`Memberships.java`** \u2014 rewrote the core logic:\n- `membershipPoints(Owner, householdSize)`: starts at 0, `+2` email present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+, `+3` for tenure over 365 days.\n- `membershipLevel(int points)`: buckets to 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\n**`Households.java`** \u2014 added `size(Owner, OwnerRepository)`, counting persisted owners sharing the `householdId` (members inclusive), reusing the repository-scan pattern already used elsewhere.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping and rewired `membershipLevel` to derive from points, via two protected helpers that pull household size from the injected `ownerRepository`. Both fields are now returned.\n\n**`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 now injects `OwnerRepository` and logs both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel` under the new scheme.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema field and updated `membershipLevel` (now max 4) with descriptions matching the new rules, so the generated DTO carries both fields.\n\nThe acceptance test's fresh owner (email + no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure) scores 3 points \u2192 level 2, as asserted.",
