    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners` (full URL `POST /petclinic/api/owners`), traced through the OfficeFloor pipeline in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`. Every step runs inside one shared `transaction` governance, so nothing commits until the very end.\n\n## 0. Endpoint guard (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition: authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Denial \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` \u2192 **403**. (Note: security is disabled by default via `petclinic.security.enable=false` in `application.properties`, so this guard is effectively off unless enabled.)\n\n## 1. `BuildOwner` \u2014 bind, validate, normalize the body\nBinds `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`. Validations, in the order they occur:\n\n- **JSR-380 bean validation** on the DTO (violation \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**):\n  - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`\n  - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`\n  - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`\n  - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n  - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n  - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n  - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")` (optional)\n  - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 ISO date (optional)\n- **Side-effect:** reads `sharesHousehold` from the request and publishes it.\n- **Side-effect:** normalizes the address (trim/collapse/upper-case; ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n- **Validation:** required-field check on `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` \u2014 any blank \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n- **Side-effect + validation:** normalizes telephone to E.164 (assumes +61) \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400**.\n- **Side-effect + validation:** normalizes email; rejects disposable domains (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` \u2192 **400**.\n- **Validation:** validates postcode against city \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` \u2192 **400**.\n- **Side-effect:** maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (via MapStruct `OwnerMapper`, ignoring `id`/`pets`).\n- **Side-effect + validation:** computes effective registration date \u2014 defaults to today, **rejects future dates** (`FutureRegistrationDateException` \u2192 **400**), and **rolls weekends forward to the next Monday** (`toBusinessDay`); sets it on the owner.\n\n## 2. `AssignHousehold` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over normalized `lastName|postcode`.\n\n## 3. `EnsureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 validation\nUnless `sharesHousehold` is true, scans all owners; if another owner has the same computed household id \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## 4. `AssignCustomerCode` \u2014 side-effect\nSets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region derived from postcode ranges, then city table, else `UNKNOWN`).\n\n## 5. `AssignNamesakeCount` \u2014 side-effect\nCounts existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive); sets `namesakeCount`.\n\n## 6. `EnsureCityCapacity` \u2014 validation\nIf the owner's city already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n\n## 7. `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit` \u2014 validation\nIf \u2265 100 owners already share this registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n\n## 8. `AssignPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 side-effect\nUnless `sharesHousehold`, finds the earliest other owner with the same `householdId` but different telephone; if found sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<that id>`, else `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n## 9. `SaveOwner` \u2014 side-effect\nPersists via Spring Data JPA `save`. (Entity-level constraints `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone and the telephone `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` are enforced here at flush; a DB integrity violation would surface as `DataIntegrityViolationException` \u2192 404 per the handler. There are **no** `@PrePersist`/lifecycle callbacks \u2014 all derived fields are set explicitly above.)\n\n## 10. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 side-effect\nComputes membership points/level and writes an SLF4J `AUDIT` info log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipPoints, membershipLevel). Logging only \u2014 no persistent audit record.\n\n## 11. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 response\nMaps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. (The mapper computes many derived response fields, several of which query `findAll()` at response time.)\n\n**Then** the single shared transaction commits.\n\n---\n\nTwo things worth flagging as you read this: the `authorize` guard is bypassed by default (security disabled in config), and the uniqueness/capacity/namesake checks all do full-table scans (`findAll`) inside the request, which is a scalability concern but not a bug per se."
  },
